# Roblox Sleepy Fish Project Rules & Context

## Project Architecture
- Framework is implemented with game-specific dependencies decoupled for easy reuse across multiple games
- All module methods on server and client use PascalCase (first letter of each word uppercase)
- NEVER use _G globals - always create and require modules for shared state or cross-script functions

## FFlags Usage
- Use FFlags via concise API: require server FFlags module once at top and call FFlags.GetBoolean(FFlags.Keys.FlagName)/GetNumber/GetString
- Do not access SharedFFlags.Options directly in server code

## Module Requirements
- All require() calls must be top-of-file, standalone lines
- Never inline require as function args or inside tables
- Group requires by service: game.ReplicatedStorage.*, game.ServerScriptService.*, then local modules
- Use absolute `game.*` paths for all requires at the top of the file
- No `script.Parent`, no WaitForChild in require, no pcall(require)
- Require all modules at the top of each Lua file using direct paths; no lazy or inline requires inside functions
- Never use os.time() use workspace:GetServerTimeNow() instead

## Project Structure
- Framework code is in framework/ directory
- Game-specific code is in game/ directory
- Uses Rojo for project management
- Follows Roblox best practices for module organization

## Development Workflow
- Always follow the established coding standards when making changes
- Test changes thoroughly before committing
- Update this file when adding new important project knowledge
